---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Custom Consulting for Founder-Led Operations | David J Forer"
description="Scoped operations and AI work for founder-led businesses that does not fit a standard audit tier. Every engagement starts with an audit.">
	<div class="mx-auto w-full text-black text-xl leading-relaxed">

		{/* Hero */}
		<section class="bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-600 to-blue-800 py-20 w-full">
			<div class="container mx-auto px-6 max-w-5xl text-center">
				<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold text-white mb-6">Custom consulting</h1>
				<p class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-blue-100 mb-8 max-w-4xl mx-auto">Some problems do not fit a package. This is where that work goes, and it still starts the same way everything else does.</p>
				<a href="/ai-readiness-and-ai-audits" class="inline-block bg-white text-blue-600 font-semibold py-4 px-8 rounded-lg text-lg hover:bg-blue-50 transition duration-300">Start with an audit</a>
			</div>
		</section>

		{/* What this is */}
		<section class="py-16 px-6">
			<div class="container mx-auto max-w-4xl">
				<h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-8">What this covers</h2>
				<div class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-6">
					<p>Most of my work is a process audit followed by a build. That covers most of what my clients need, and it is priced and scoped before anything starts.</p>

					<p>Then there is the other kind. Problems like these: a 14-person insurance brokerage that already documented its renewals process 2 years ago and cannot get anyone to follow the doc. A design studio moving off one project tool onto another when intake was never defined, so both tools hold the same mess in different shapes. A founder who has quietly become the only person who knows how quoting works, and has 3 months before a key hire starts.</p>

					<p>Work like that gets scoped from what I find.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		{/* Who */}
		<section class="py-16 px-6 bg-gray-50">
			<div class="container mx-auto max-w-4xl">
				<h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-8">Who I work with</h2>
				<div class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-6">
					<p>Founder-led service businesses. Usually 5 to 20 people, somewhere between $1M and $5M in revenue, with no dedicated operations lead. Revenue is fine. The founder is the constraint.</p>

					<p>That last part matters more than the revenue number. If every real decision still routes through one person, adding tools or headcount tends to move the bottleneck rather than remove it. That is the pattern I know best and the one I am most useful on.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		{/* How it starts */}
		<section class="py-16 px-6">
			<div class="container mx-auto max-w-4xl">
				<h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-8">How it starts</h2>
				<div class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-6">
					<p>With an audit. Always.</p>

					<p>I do not quote custom work off a discovery call, because a discovery call tells me what a founder believes is broken, and that is rarely the whole picture. The audit extracts how the work actually moves today: what comes in, what gets decided, what gets handed off, and where it stalls. Scope comes out of that, in writing, with a fixed price before anything gets built.</p>

					<p>If the audit shows the problem fits one of the standard engagements, I will say so and you get the cheaper path.</p>

					<div class="mt-10">
						<a href="/ai-readiness-and-ai-audits" class="inline-block bg-blue-600 text-white font-semibold py-4 px-8 rounded-lg text-lg hover:bg-blue-700 transition duration-300">See how the audit works</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		{/* Boundaries */}
		<section class="py-16 px-6 bg-gray-50">
			<div class="container mx-auto max-w-4xl">
				<h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-8">What I turn down</h2>
				<div class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-6">
					<p>Worth knowing before you book a call.</p>

					<ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-3 ml-4">
						<li>Monthly retainers with no defined scope. Engagements are fixed-scope with a defined end.</li>
						<li>Staff augmentation. I am one person and I am not a substitute for a hire you need to make.</li>
						<li>Training a model on your data. There is almost always a cheaper answer, and it usually starts with fixing the process feeding it.</li>
						<li>Anything where the answer is already decided and the work is to justify it.</li>
					</ul>

					<p>Saying that up front saves us both a call.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		{/* NDA note */}
		<section class="py-16 px-6 bg-blue-600 text-white">
			<div class="container mx-auto max-w-4xl text-center">
				<h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-8">Why there are no client names here</h2>
				<div class="text-lg leading-relaxed space-y-6">
					<p>Client work runs under NDA. That covers the process maps, the systems, and usually the fact of the engagement itself, so you will not find logos or named case studies on this site. Operations work touches how a business actually makes money and who it depends on. Founders are right to want that kept quiet, and I would rather have their trust than a testimonial slider.</p>

					<p>What I can point you at is the thinking. The method comes from years of audits and operational work, most recently at Spyglass Ops. The writing is public and there is a lot of it.</p>

					<div class="mt-10">
						<a href="/blog" class="inline-block bg-white text-blue-600 font-semibold py-4 px-8 rounded-lg text-lg hover:bg-blue-50 transition duration-300">Read the writing</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		{/* CTA */}
		<section class="py-16 px-6">
			<div class="container mx-auto max-w-4xl text-center">
				<h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-6">If this sounds like your situation</h2>
				<p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-10">Book 30 minutes. I will tell you whether an audit is worth your money before you spend any of it.</p>
				<a href="https://calendly.com/david-j-forer/30min" class="inline-block bg-blue-600 text-white font-semibold py-4 px-8 rounded-lg text-lg hover:bg-blue-700 transition duration-300">Book a call</a>
			</div>
		</section>

	</div>
</Layout>
